      <h3>Question 1 — Universal Approximation Theorem</h3>

      <p>
        Which statement best describes the Universal Approximation Theorem?
      </p>

      <ol type="A">
        <li>Every neural network always achieves zero training error.</li>
        <li>A suitable network with sufficient hidden units can approximate a broad class of continuous functions on a compact domain.</li>
        <li>Every network needs exactly one hidden neuron.</li>
