      <ul>
        <li><code>loss.backward()</code> calculates gradients.</li>
        <li><code>optimizer.step()</code> updates parameters.</li>
        <li><code>optimizer.zero_grad()</code> clears existing gradients.</li>
        <li><code>model.train()</code> selects training mode.</li>
        <li><code>model.eval()</code> selects evaluation mode.</li>
        <li><code>torch.no_grad()</code> disables gradient tracking in a context.</li>
        <li><code>nn.CrossEntropyLoss</code> normally takes logits and integer class labels.</li>
        <li><code>nn.BCEWithLogitsLoss</code> takes logits and compatible floating-point targets.</li>
        <li><code>nn.MSELoss</code> measures mean squared numerical error.</li>
